# Copy this file to `.env` in the same directory and fill in your key:
#
#     cp example/.env.example example/.env
#
# `.env` is git-ignored. Never commit a real key.
#
# ── Where to get a key ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. Create an account at https://platform.decart.ai
# 2. Open the API Keys section of the dashboard
# 3. Generate a key and paste it below
#
# Permanent keys are prefixed `dct_`. Short-lived client tokens are prefixed
# `ek_` — either works here.
#
# ── DEVELOPMENT ONLY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Shipping a permanent `dct_` key inside an app binary is not safe: anyone can
# extract it from the APK or IPA. It is fine for this example app running on
# your own device, and it is what makes local testing painless — but a
# production app must fetch a short-lived client token (`ek_…`) from its own
# backend instead. See:
#
#   https://docs.platform.decart.ai/getting-started/client-tokens
#
# The plugin API is identical either way: whatever string you pass to
# `DecartVton().initialize(apiKey: ...)` is used as-is.

DECART_API_KEY=
